From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:42:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: unmap exported dma-buf sg tables with the original
 entry count

nv_dma_buf_unmap_pages() passed sgt->nents, the count dma_map_sg_attrs()
returned, to dma_unmap_sg_attrs(). The DMA API wants the count that was
passed to dma_map_sg_attrs() (sgt->orig_nents); the returned count can be
smaller when an IOMMU merges segments. dma-direct and the dma-iommu unmap
happen to cope, other implementations need not.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dmabuf.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dmabuf.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dmabuf.c
index 8682049c..3bf02e8a 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dmabuf.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dmabuf.c
@@ -705,7 +705,8 @@ nv_dma_buf_unmap_pages(
         return;
     }
 
-    dma_unmap_sg_attrs(dev, sgt->sgl, sgt->nents,
+    // Unmap takes the count passed to dma_map_sg_attrs(), not the one it returned
+    dma_unmap_sg_attrs(dev, sgt->sgl, sgt->orig_nents,
                        DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL, DMA_ATTR_SKIP_CPU_SYNC);
 }
 
